-- title:
--   Regularity ascends to polynomial and multivariate polynomial rings
-- statement:
--   This module proves, entirely in terms of Mathlib's predicates `IsRegularLocalRing` and `IsRegularRing`, that regularity is stable under adjoining a polynomial variable. Three transport lemmas come first: if two prime ideals $I=J$ of a commutative semiring $A$ agree, then an $A$-algebra that is a localization at $A\setminus I$ is one at $A\setminus J$; and for a prime $J$ of a commutative ring $A$ and an $A$-algebra $S$ with $S$ a localization of $A$ at $J^{\mathrm{c}}$, regularity of $S$ and of `Localization.AtPrime J` are equivalent (each direction stated separately).
--
--   The substantive chain concerns a prime $P$ of $R[X]$ and its contraction $P\cap R$ (written `P.under R`). First, for a domain $D$ and a prime $Q$ of $D[X]$ such that $C d\in Q$ forces $d=0$, the local ring $D[X]_Q$ is regular: $D[X]_Q$ is a localization of $\operatorname{Frac}(D)[X]$ at the prime generated by $Q$, where regularity of localizations of a polynomial ring over a field is available. Applying this to $R[X]/(P\cap R)R[X]\cong (R/(P\cap R))[X]$ gives regularity of the localization at the image of $P$, provided that image is prime; consequently the quotient of $R[X]_P$ by the ideal generated by the image of $C(P\cap R)$ — the closed fibre of $R_{P\cap R}\to R[X]_P$ — is a regular local ring. If $R$ is a regular ring, then $R[X]$ is free, hence flat, over $R$, the map $R_{P\cap R}\to R[X]_P$ is a flat local homomorphism, and flat local ascent yields regularity of $R[X]_P$; since $R[X]$ is Noetherian, $R[X]$ is a regular ring.
--
--   Two corollaries follow: $k[X_1,\dots,X_n]$ is a regular ring for a field $k$ and every $n$, by induction on $n$, which together with smoothness of $k\to k[X_1,\dots,X_n]$ gives the conjunction of `Algebra.Smooth` and regularity of all stalks; and $\mathbb{Z}[X]$ is a regular ring.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** All notions used are Mathlib's (`IsRegularRing`, `IsRegularLocalRing`, `Localization.AtPrime`, `Ideal.under`, `Ideal.polynomialQuotientEquivQuotientPolynomial`, `Algebra.Smooth`); nothing new is defined. The ascent step invoked, [`RegularFlatLocalAscent.isRegularLocalRing_of_flat_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient`](../def/Mathlib_RingTheory_RegularLocalRingFlatLocalAscent.html#L141) (regularity of a flat local extension from regularity of its closed fibre), belongs to the project's own development.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These results supply the commutative-algebra input that polynomial algebras over a field or over $\mathbb{Z}$ have regular local rings at all primes, which is the model case in the argument that a smooth algebra over a field has regular stalks (the predicate [`SmoothFieldFiberRegularStalksInput`](../def/Mathlib_RingTheory_SmoothAlgebraOverFieldRegularStalks.html#L7)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_Mathlib_RingTheory_KmfloorsFiberPolynomialRegularAscent.lean

